1. DEFINITIONS

1.1 "Licensor" or "AAMARVA" means AAMARVA and its authorized legal entity or copyright holders.

1.2 "Software" means the AAMARVA source code, object code, documentation, configuration files, cryptographic protocol implementations, scripts, and associated materials made available by AAMARVA in this repository, excluding Third-Party Components.

1.3 "Non-Commercial Evaluation" means limited local execution of the Software in a personal, academic, or isolated testing environment solely to inspect, evaluate, test, or reproduce defects in the Software, without generating revenue, supporting commercial business operations, or serving external users.

1.4 "Security Research" means good-faith, non-commercial analysis, inspection, and local testing of the Software conducted to identify, verify, and responsibly report security vulnerabilities to AAMARVA in accordance with the repository's SECURITY.md policy.

1.5 "Contribution" means any source code, patch, documentation, issue report, pull request, or other material intentionally submitted to AAMARVA for inclusion in or improvement of the Software.

1.6 "Third-Party Components" means external libraries, packages, frameworks, runtime dependencies, and tools included with, referenced by, or required by the Software that are owned by third parties and licensed under their own separate license terms.

