Subject to your continuous compliance with the terms and restrictions of this License, AAMARVA grants you a limited, revocable, non-exclusive, non-transferable, non-sublicensable, royalty-free permission solely to perform the following activities:

2.1 Viewing and Inspecting Source Code: You may view, read, and inspect the publicly available source code of the Software.

2.2 Architecture and Implementation Review: You may review and analyze the architecture, cryptographic design, implementation, and documentation of the Software.

2.3 Non-Commercial Security Research: You may conduct non-commercial Security Research and vulnerability analysis on the Software, provided such research complies with Section 2.7 and the repository's SECURITY.md guidelines, does not target production infrastructure without separate written authorization, and does not access, extract, or disclose real user data.

2.4 Bug and Vulnerability Reporting: You may report software bugs, defects, and security vulnerabilities to AAMARVA through the designated reporting channels.

2.5 Issue Submission and Proposed Improvements: You may submit bug reports, architectural feedback, issues, and proposed improvements to the repository.

2.6 Pull Requests and Contributions: You may fork the repository within the hosting platform and create local modifications solely as necessary to prepare and submit pull requests to AAMARVA under the repository's contribution terms (see CONTRIBUTING.md).

2.7 Limited Local Execution: You may compile, build, and execute the Software locally in an isolated, non-production environment solely for Non-Commercial Evaluation, automated testing, and authorized Security Research.

2.8 Bug Reproduction: You may execute and test the Software locally to reproduce bugs and verify fixes for legitimate testing and contribution purposes.

